        Example of flow over an embankment shaped weir.
        The table will not be echoed to the output file.
 
EMBANKQ
TABID=   500 CSHIFT= 0.00      
;     The tables referenced here must have been input prior to the
;     EMBANKQ command.  By creating the proper tables you can use
;     EMBANKQ to compute the flow over sloping weirs that are other
;     than embankment shaped.  See example later in this input.
PLCWTB= 9994
GLCWTB= 9995
PHCWTB= 9996
GHCWTB= 9997
*     If the entries for the next two tables are left blank, FEQUTL
*     will produce a table of type 2 because it cannot compute
*     submergence.  Such a table would be used as a downstream boundary
*     condition if you were satisfied that nothing downstream would cause
*     submerged flow over the weir or embankment.
PSUBTB= 9998
GSUBTB= 9999
LABEL= MTPPOOL TO PENPOOL
;     Labels for tables are highly recommended.
    OFFSET     CREST     WIDTH  APPROACH SURFACE
      0.0       11.8       25.       9.0 PAVED
    235.0       11.4                 8.9
    630.0       11.3                 8.7
    995.0       11.3                 8.4
   1410.0       11.7                 8.2
   1780.0       11.7                 8.0 END
UPSTREAM HEADS TO USE IN COMPUTING THE TABLE
0.01
0.05
0.10
0.15
0.20
0.30
0.40
0.75
1.0
-1.
 
 
        Example of SEWER option.  SEWER produces a cross section table
        complete with top slot for a round conduit.
 
SEWER
TABID=   636  NOOUT
DIAMETER= 3.0
NSIDES=  30
WSLOT= 0.01
HSLOT=1.0
N= 0.020
 
 
        Example of MULPIPES option.  MULPIPES produces a cross section
        table for multiple round conduits.
        The BOTT option permits the pipes to be a slightly different
        elevations.  Be wary of computing a single table for use in the
        CULVERT command if the pipes elevations differ by a large fraction
        of the smaller diameter.  In this case, the flow type may differ for
        each pipe and aggregating the pipes into one table may
        misrepresent the flow details.
 
MULPIPES
;     A positive table number requests that FEQUTL force the conveyance
;     in the pipes to be monotone increasing.  This means that the maximum
;     conveyance propagates to the higher depths.  This may or may not
;     be realistic.
;
;     If the slot is small enough, FEQUTL will put a standard slot
;     height of 500 feet on each table of closed conduit.  This is
;     after the table has been computed.  Thus the slot height given
;     in HSLOT need only be high enough to go over the top of the
;     largest conduit.  The same rules apply to SEWER and MULCON.
;
TABID=   650
NSIDES=  20
WSLOT= 0.01
HSLOT= 1.0
NPIPES=    3
DIAM=       3.5       4.0       3.5
BOTT=       0.5       0.0       0.5
ROUG=     0.020     0.020     0.020
        Example of MULCON option.  The MULCON option is a generalization
        of the MULPIPES option and therefore can do all that MULPIPES can
        do and more.
 
        RCPA - reinforced concrete pipe arch
        NHE - nominal horizontal elliptical
        NVE - nominal vertical elliptical
        TE - true elliptical
        CIRC - circular
 
MULCON
;     Negative table number forces FEQUTL to compute the conveyance
;     for the conduit including any decrease as the water surface
;     approaches the top of the conduit.  Messages about a decrease
;     in conveyance will be issued at each point which represents
;     a decrease as the depth increases.
TABID=  -107  OUT1
WSLOT= 0.01
HSLOT= 15.0
NPIPES=    5
TYPE:      RCPA      NHE        NVE      CIRC        TE
SPAN:                         12.00     12.00      3.15
RISE:      2.00     12.00                2.00     12.00
BOTT:       1.0       2.0       0.0       0.4       0.8
ROUG:      0.02      0.02      0.02      0.02      0.02
 
        Example of MULCON computing a cross section table for
        a box culvert.
 
MULCON
TABID=  -999 SAVE12  NOOUT
WSLOT= 0.01
HSLOT= 25.0
NPIPES=    1
TYPE:       BOX
SPAN:        3.
RISE:        3.
BOTT:       0.0
ROUG:     0.018
 
 
